Discussion:

The resulting top-twenty bigrams were the same for both the chi-square and pmi methods.
I suspect that I made a mistake in my implementation of the chi-square function. Most likely
I needed to construct a contingency table but I was unsure if that was necessary. After seeing the results, I
belive that is what was wrong with the implementation.

Both methods seem to identify a few collocations. However, since the lists are both identical, I can't determine
which method was better without further investigation.